      ":question/worked-solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{1}{2x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](generate/scratch/17592186068814/plots/51c8fd38e126afd05e67e9e538dd834692bb47d55a0f6189b99c1e8e5cb92604.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{2x}.$\n\n![](generate/scratch/17592186068814/plots/9e3d5479252e4353ba3cbf9db2b71b53f0cdd38c7c3568089677bc6b8819e10d.png)",
